@namespace AuthWithAdmin.Client.Pages.Planning

@*
    PlanningItemChip — the final Calendar's event chip
    (Motiva Student Calendar final.dc.html, `chip()`).

    One chip shape shared by Month, the Week view's כל היום band and the mobile
    Agenda, so the five planning types read identically wherever they appear.

    THE REFERENCE'S CHIP IS A DOT, NOT AN ICON
    r7 on the type tint, label in the TYPE's own ink at 600 11px/1.35, led by a
    5px dot of the same ink. The per-kind glyph the earlier board used is gone:
    at 11px five stroked glyphs are indistinguishable, and the reference proves
    the dot carries the type on its own once the label is tinted with it.

    The label is `HH:mm · title` for an item with a work block and the bare
    title otherwise — verbatim the reference's own `label` expression.

    Done and overdue are Motiva's, not the reference's: the prototype has no
    completion or lateness state to draw. Both are kept — they are working
    behaviour, and dropping them to match a static file would lose information
    the student needs.
*@

<button type="button"
        class="pl-chip pl-k-@PlanningKinds.Slug(Item.Kind) @(Item.IsDone ? "pl-chip-done" : "") @(Item.IsOverdue ? "pl-chip-overdue" : "") @(Relaxed ? "pl-chip-relaxed" : "")"
        style="@PlanningKinds.PaletteStyle(Item.Kind)"
        title="@Tooltip"
        @onclick="HandleClick"
        @onclick:stopPropagation="true">

    <span class="pl-chip-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>

    <span class="pl-chip-text">
        <span class="pl-chip-title">
            @if (Item.HasTime)
            {
                <span class="pl-chip-time" dir="ltr">@Item.StartTime</span><span> · </span>
            }
            @Item.Title
        </span>
        @if (Relaxed)
        {
            <span class="pl-chip-meta">@PlanningKinds.Label(Item.Kind) · @Item.StatusLabel</span>
        }
    </span>

    @if (Item.IsDone)
    {
        <svg class="pl-chip-check" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
             stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M5 12.5 9.5 17 19 7"></path>
        </svg>
    }
</button>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public PlanningItem Item { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>Week view: two lines (title + type · status). Month: one line.
    /// The Design's month cell caps at 104px with two chips, which leaves no
    /// room for a second line — the Week column has the height to spare.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Relaxed { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public EventCallback<PlanningItem> OnOpen { get; set; }

    private string Tooltip =>
        $"{PlanningKinds.Label(Item.Kind)} · {Item.Title} · {Item.Date:dd.MM.yyyy} · {Item.StatusLabel}";

    private Task HandleClick() => OnOpen.InvokeAsync(Item);
}
